      "worked": "The final digit must be 0 or 5.\n\nEnding in 0: the first three digits have 5, 4 and 3 choices respectively.\n$$N_0=5\\times4\\times3=60.$$\nEnding in 5: the leading digit has 4 choices because it cannot be 0 or 5. The next two digits have 4 and 3 choices respectively.\n$$N_5=4\\times4\\times3=48.$$\nThe cases are disjoint, so\n$$N=60+48=108.$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
